@startuml fractals-workspace-architecture
' =====================================================================
' Fractal Workspace Application Architecture Diagram (2025 - Production)
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' This diagram illustrates the complete modular, layered architecture of the
' Fractal Workspace application v1.0.0, including all four tabs:
' - Fractal Generator
' - Box Counter
' - Image Compare
' - Tumor Detection
' Each package and class is annotated for clarity and maintainability.
' =====================================================================

scale 4096 width

title Fractal Workspace v1.0.0 - Complete Architecture (2025)

' Define UX-friendly colors (PlantUML syntax)
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor<<UI>> #B3C7F7
  BackgroundColor<<BOX>> #FFD6E0
  BackgroundColor<<FRACTAL>> #FFF7B2
  BackgroundColor<<UTIL>> #B2F7C1
  BackgroundColor<<TUMOR>> #FFE4B5
  BackgroundColor<<HANDLER>> #E0FFFF
}

note as N1
  LEGEND:
  [Soft Blue]     UI Layer: Main window with 4 tabs (Fractal, Box Counter, Image Compare, Tumor Detection)
  [Soft Pink]     Box Counting Layer: Helpers, utils, and comparison dialog
  [Soft Yellow]   Fractal Logic Layer: 6 fractal generation algorithms
  [Soft Peach]    Tumor Detection Layer: YOLOv5-based medical image analysis
  [Soft Cyan]     Handler Layer: Event handlers and utility functions
  [Soft Green]    Utility Layer: External libraries (numpy, cv2, matplotlib, PyQt6)
end note

' ---------------------------
'         UI LAYER (4 TABS)
' ---------------------------
package "UI Layer" <<UI>> {
    class MainWindow {
        ' Constants
        +APP_TITLE: str
        +APP_VERSION: str
        +DEFAULT_FRACTAL_TYPE: str
        +DEFAULT_RESOLUTION: str
        
        ' Tab Setup Methods
        +__init__()
        +setup_fractal_tab()
        +setup_box_counter_tab()
        +setup_image_compare_tab()
        +setup_tumor_detection_tab()
        
        ' Fractal Generator Tab Methods
        +generate_fractal_threaded()
        +save_fractal()
        +combo_frac_type_changed()
        +combo_resolution_changed()
        +combo_color_scheme_changed()
        +edit_max_iter_changed()
        +edit_power_changed()
        +edit_c_real_changed()
        +edit_c_imag_changed()
        
        ' Box Counter Tab Methods
        +bc_select_image()
        +bc_apply_roi_size()
        +bc_update_display()
        +bc_compute_roi()
        
        ' Image Compare Tab Methods
        +handle_image_label_drop()
        +handle_image_label_double_click()
        +swap_image_compare()
        +reset_image_compare()
        +process_image_compare()
        +add_compare_step()
        
        ' State Variables
        -fractal_type: str
        -resolution: str
        -color_scheme: str
        -max_iter: int
        -power: float
        -bc_image: ndarray
        -bc_roi_size: int
        -_img1_data: ndarray
        -_img2_data: ndarray
        -_compare_steps: list
        -tumor_images: list
        -tumor_results: list
    }
    
    class ROIImageLabel {
        +parent: MainWindow
        +mousePressEvent()
        +resizeEvent()
        +paintEvent()
    }
    
    class ScalableLabel {
        +setPixmap()
        +resizeEvent()
        +dragEnterEvent()
        +dragLeaveEvent()
        +dropEvent()
        -_original_pixmap: QPixmap
        -_drag_active: bool
    }
    
    note right of MainWindow
      MainWindow (v1.0.0) is the central application window.
      It manages all 4 tabs with production-ready features:
      
      1. Fractal Generator: Create 6 types of fractals
      2. Box Counter: Compute fractal dimensions via ROI
      3. Image Compare: Compare 2 images with drag-drop support
      4. Tumor Detection: YOLOv5-based medical analysis
      
      Features: Type hints, error handling, constants,
      comprehensive docstrings, input validation.
    end note
    
    note right of ScalableLabel
      Custom QLabel for Image Compare tab
      with drag-and-drop support, visual feedback,
      automatic scaling, and loading spinner.
    end note
}

' ---------------------------
'   BOX COUNTING LAYER
' ---------------------------
package "Box Counting Layer" <<BOX>> {
    class BoxCounterHelpers {
        +select_image(parent): tuple
        +apply_roi_size(parent, roi_text): int
        +update_display(parent)
        +compute_roi(parent, x, y)
    }
    
    class BoxCounterUtils {
        +load_image_for_compare(parent, which, img1_label, img2_label, path): ndarray
        +box_counting(image, min_box_size, max_box_size): tuple
        +fractal_dim(image): tuple
    }
    
    class BoxCounterCompareDialog {
        +show_boxcount_comparison_dialog(parent, img1, img2, np_to_pixmap)
        +export_as_image()
        +export_as_pdf()
    }
    
    note right of BoxCounterHelpers
      High-level helpers for Box Counter tab:
      - Image selection with GIF support
      - ROI size validation
      - Display updates with fractal dimension overlay
      - ROI computation delegation
    end note
    
    note right of BoxCounterUtils
      Core box counting algorithms:
      - box_counting(): Multi-scale grid overlay
      - fractal_dim(): Complete pipeline with
        preprocessing, skeletonization, log-log fit
      - load_image_for_compare(): Supports multiple formats
    end note
    
    note right of BoxCounterCompareDialog
      Stepwise comparison dialog:
      - Preprocesses both images
      - Overlays grids at multiple scales
      - Plots log-log graphs
      - Computes slopes (fractal dimensions)
      - Displays results with interpretation
      - Export to PNG/PDF
    end note
}

' ---------------------------
'     FRACTAL LOGIC LAYER
' ---------------------------
package "Fractal Logic Layer" <<FRACTAL>> {
    class Mandelbrot {
        +width: int
        +height: int
        +max_iter: int
        +power: float
        +generate(): ndarray
    }
    
    class Julia {
        +width: int
        +height: int
        +max_iter: int
        +c_real: float
        +c_imag: float
        +generate(): ndarray
    }
    
    class BurningShip {
        +width: int
        +height: int
        +max_iter: int
        +power: float
        +generate(): ndarray
    }
    
    class NewtonFractal {
        +width: int
        +height: int
        +max_iter: int
        +n: int
        +generate(): ndarray
    }
    
    class BarnsleyFern {
        +width: int
        +height: int
        +num_points: int
        +generate(): ndarray
    }
    
    class SierpinskiTriangle {
        +width: int
        +height: int
        +num_points: int
        +generate(): ndarray
    }
    
    class FractalInfoUtil {
        +get_fractal_info(fractal_type): str
    }
    
    note right
      6 fractal algorithms, each implementing:
      - Configurable parameters
      - generate() method returning numpy array
      - Optimized computation using numpy
      
      FractalInfoUtil provides LaTeX formulas
      and descriptions for each fractal type.
    end note
}

' ---------------------------
'   TUMOR DETECTION LAYER
' ---------------------------
package "Tumor Detection Layer" <<TUMOR>> {
    class TumorDetector {
        +model_path: str
        +device: str
        +load_model()
        +detect(image): ndarray
    }
    
    class DetectionWorker {
        +run()
        +signals: WorkerSignals
    }
    
    note right
      YOLOv5-based tumor detection:
      - 3 models: Axial, Coronal, Sagittal
      - GPU/CPU support
      - Threaded execution via DetectionWorker
      - Bounding box overlay on detected regions
    end note
}

' ---------------------------
'      HANDLER LAYER
' ---------------------------
package "Handler Layer" <<HANDLER>> {
    class FractalHandlers {
        +combo_frac_type_changed(parent, fractal_type)
        +combo_resolution_changed(parent, resolution)
        +combo_color_scheme_changed(parent, scheme)
        +edit_max_iter_changed(parent)
        +edit_power_changed(parent)
        +edit_c_real_changed(parent)
        +edit_c_imag_changed(parent)
        +generate_fractal_threaded(parent)
        +save_fractal(parent)
        +np_to_pixmap(image): QPixmap
    }
    
    class TumorHandlers {
        +handle_tumor_image_double_click(parent, idx)
        +run_tumor_detection(parent, idx)
    }
    
    note right
      Event handlers separated from UI:
      - FractalHandlers: All fractal generation logic
      - TumorHandlers: Tumor detection workflows
      - Clean separation of concerns
      - Testable business logic
    end note
}

' ---------------------------
'        UTILITY LAYER
' ---------------------------
package "Utility Layer" <<UTIL>> {
    class numpy {
        Arrays, linear algebra,
        mathematical operations
    }
    
    class matplotlib {
        Plotting, colormaps,
        figure rendering
    }
    
    class cv2 {
        Image I/O, preprocessing,
        thresholding, morphology
    }
    
    class skimage {
        Skeletonization,
        advanced image processing
    }
    
    class PyQt6 {
        GUI framework, widgets,
        layouts, signals/slots
    }
    
    class torch {
        YOLOv5 model loading,
        tensor operations, inference
    }
    
    note right
      External dependencies:
      - numpy: Core array operations
      - matplotlib: Visualization
      - cv2 (OpenCV): Image processing
      - skimage: Scientific image analysis
      - PyQt6: Modern GUI framework
      - torch: Deep learning for tumor detection
    end note
}

' ---------------------------
'        RELATIONSHIPS
' ---------------------------

' MainWindow to Fractal Generators
MainWindow --> Mandelbrot : generates
MainWindow --> Julia : generates
MainWindow --> BurningShip : generates
MainWindow --> NewtonFractal : generates
MainWindow --> BarnsleyFern : generates
MainWindow --> SierpinskiTriangle : generates
MainWindow --> FractalInfoUtil : displays info

' MainWindow to Box Counting Components
MainWindow --> ROIImageLabel : owns
MainWindow --> ScalableLabel : creates
MainWindow --> BoxCounterHelpers : delegates to
MainWindow --> BoxCounterUtils : uses
MainWindow --> BoxCounterCompareDialog : launches

' MainWindow to Tumor Detection
MainWindow --> TumorDetector : uses
MainWindow --> DetectionWorker : creates threads

' MainWindow to Handlers
MainWindow --> FractalHandlers : delegates events
MainWindow --> TumorHandlers : delegates events

' Box Counting Internal Relationships
ROIImageLabel ..> MainWindow : parent reference
ScalableLabel ..> MainWindow : parent reference
BoxCounterHelpers --> BoxCounterUtils : calls
BoxCounterHelpers --> MainWindow : updates state
BoxCounterCompareDialog --> BoxCounterUtils : calls box_counting()
BoxCounterCompareDialog --> MainWindow : updates UI

' Tumor Detection Internal
TumorDetector --> torch : uses
DetectionWorker --> TumorDetector : runs detection

' Handlers to Core Logic
FractalHandlers --> Mandelbrot : creates
FractalHandlers --> Julia : creates
FractalHandlers --> BurningShip : creates
FractalHandlers --> NewtonFractal : creates
FractalHandlers --> BarnsleyFern : creates
FractalHandlers --> SierpinskiTriangle : creates
TumorHandlers --> TumorDetector : invokes

' Dependencies on Utilities
BoxCounterUtils ..> numpy : array operations
BoxCounterUtils ..> cv2 : image processing
BoxCounterUtils ..> skimage : skeletonization

Mandelbrot ..> numpy : computation
Mandelbrot ..> matplotlib : not used directly
Julia ..> numpy : computation
BurningShip ..> numpy : computation
NewtonFractal ..> numpy : computation
BarnsleyFern ..> numpy : computation
SierpinskiTriangle ..> numpy : computation

MainWindow ..> PyQt6 : inherits from
MainWindow ..> matplotlib : via FigureCanvas
MainWindow ..> cv2 : image display
MainWindow ..> numpy : data handling

TumorDetector ..> cv2 : preprocessing
TumorDetector ..> numpy : array handling

FractalHandlers ..> matplotlib : plotting
FractalHandlers ..> numpy : data handling

' ---------------------------
'         FOOTER
' ---------------------------
note bottom
  ==== How to Read This Diagram ====
  
  ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW:
  - 6 logical layers with clear separation of concerns
  - 4 tabs in MainWindow: Fractal Generator, Box Counter, Image Compare, Tumor Detection
  - Modular design enables independent testing and maintenance
  
  KEY FEATURES (v1.0.0):
  - Type-hinted methods for better IDE support
  - Comprehensive docstrings following Google style
  - Production-ready error handling and validation
  - Constants extracted for maintainability
  - Drag-and-drop UI with visual feedback
  - Multi-threaded operations for responsiveness
  
  RELATIONSHIP TYPES:
  - Solid arrows (-->): Ownership or direct usage
  - Dotted arrows (..>): Dependency or reference
  
  TABS FUNCTIONALITY:
  1. Fractal Generator: 6 fractals, 12 color schemes, adjustable parameters
  2. Box Counter: Interactive ROI selection, fractal dimension computation
  3. Image Compare: Drag-drop images, box counting comparison, step-by-step results
  4. Tumor Detection: 3 YOLOv5 models for medical image analysis
end note

@enduml